' UI-42 at a service and the trader (`preset classic ai none seed 3 start 0
' window 640x480`, New Sandez; as it is and with `newgfx off`): the pub's
' table and the trader's exchange resized, switched to fullscreen and back,
' and clicked after each change. `sceneclick` is in the scene's own
' coordinates — the trader's 470 wide when the game is 450 or wider,
' else 320 — made a window pixel when the step is taken.
' v12_viewport_trade_still (every resize and switch a `resize 640x480`)
' must give the same game lines and save. The narrow trader (game under 450
' wide) shows one side and takes the side from the pointer, so the pointer
' is put on the player's side (`scenemove`) after each change.
press escape             ' Back closes the manual v1.2 opens on a new game's first world map
mapclick 75,303          ' into New Sandez
wait 60
day
day                      ' thirsty
mapclick 309,264         ' the pub
wait 120
esc                      ' the pub's film
wait 5
snap pub_640
resize 1280x720
wait 3
snap pub_1280
sceneclick 88,119        ' the bottle onto the table, after the resize
wait 3
snap pub_1280_table
f11
wait 3
snap pub_full
deal                     ' served in fullscreen
wait 3
f11
wait 3
resize 600x449           ' the computed minimum: 320 x 200
wait 3
snap pub_600
esc                      ' out
mapmove 5,5              ' the pointer off the place's people: one under it stops
wait 10                  ' (Location.HoverCharacter), and a resize moves what it is over
mapclick 224,305         ' the trader: film_05
wait 120
press space              ' the film closed: the trader
wait 10
snap trader_640           ' 341 wide: the narrow trader, one side at a time
resize 1920x1080         ' 512 wide: the wide layout (470), both sides
wait 3
snap trader_1920
resize 1280x720          ' 455: still wide (TraderScene's 450)
scenemove 60,120         ' the pointer put on the player's side again: it
wait 3                   ' stays on its window pixel through a resize, which
snap trader_1280         ' is another scene point now (the narrow side follows it)
rsceneclick 88,119       ' the first thing set aside, in the wide layout's coordinates
wait 3
snap trader_1280_aside
sceneclick 172,16        ' and back to the pack
wait 3
resize 600x449           ' the computed minimum: 320 x 200, narrow
scenemove 60,120
wait 3
snap trader_600
rsceneclick 88,119       ' aside again at the smallest size
wait 3
snap trader_600_aside
f11
scenemove 60,120
wait 3
snap trader_full
sceneclick 172,16        ' back, in fullscreen
wait 3
snap trader_full_back
f11
scenemove 60,120
wait 3
snap trader_back
esc                      ' leave
wait 10
resize 640x480
wait 3
save
quit
